Argentina is officially the only country from Latin America still standing in the 2026 FIFA World Cup.&nbsp;Led by soccer star Lionel Messi, the South American team is one of the eight headed to the quarterfinals, alongside France, Morocco, Spain, Belgium, Norway, England and Switzerland.&nbsp;

